@startuml use_cases
' FlakeTrace use case diagram -- whole committed project (FR-1..FR-7).
' Source: docs/02-Requirements/functional.md, non-functional.md, scope-boundary.md.
' <<iteration 1>> marks a use case FlakeTrace delivers today, on main. Unmarked
' use cases/notes are committed scope for a later iteration (docs/00-Meta/roadmap.md;
' Chapter 10) -- never invented, never the GATED/STRETCH tier (CDR, JUnit 5, Gradle,
' etc. are out of this diagram entirely).
skinparam dpi 200
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 50
top to bottom direction

actor Developer as dev
actor "CI Pipeline" as ci

rectangle FlakeTrace {
  usecase "UC1: Submit Diagnosis Request\n(pinned commit, module, target test, budget)" as UC1 <<iteration 1>>
  usecase "UC7: Invoke via CLI,\nConsume Exit Code" as UC7 <<iteration 1>>
  usecase "UC2: Run Ordered Test Replay\n(one fresh JVM per order)" as UC2 <<iteration 1>>
  usecase "UC3: Collect Resource Evidence\n(static fields, system properties)" as UC3 <<iteration 1>>
  usecase "UC4: Search for Polluter" as UC4 <<iteration 1>>
  usecase "UC5: Minimise & Verify Sequence\n(1-minimal, Wilson interval)" as UC5 <<iteration 1>>
  usecase "UC6: Receive Certificate\n(Verified / Candidate / Unresolved)" as UC6 <<iteration 1>>
}

dev --> UC1
dev --> UC7
ci --> UC1
ci --> UC7

UC1 ..> UC2 : <<include>>
UC2 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
UC3 ..> UC4 : <<include>>
UC4 ..> UC5 : <<include>>
UC5 ..> UC6 : <<include>>

note right of UC2
  FR-2 commits to a **sandboxed container**;
  Iteration 1 runs one fresh JVM natively
  (no container yet) -- **planned, a later
  iteration (Chapter 10)**.
end note

note right of UC3
  FR-3 commits to 3 resource families.
  Iteration 1: static fields + system
  properties only. Filesystem paths
  -- **planned, a later iteration (Ch. 10)**.
end note

note right of UC4
  FR-4 commits to 2 search policies.
  Iteration 1 ships ranked one-by-one
  (+ delta-debugging minimisation).
  Cost-aware adaptive policy
  -- **planned, a later iteration (Ch. 10)**.
end note

note right of UC7
  NFR-2's "install on clean Linux
  from documentation, third party
  verifies" is a stated **Final-2
  exit requirement**, not
  claimed for Iteration 1.
end note

legend right
  <<iteration 1>>  delivered on main today
  plain note       committed scope, not yet built (a later iteration, Ch. 10)
endlegend
@enduml
